      "id": 1,
      "text": "King Arthur Park Mobile Home Park began in 1973 as a land‑lease community to provide affordable housing in the rapidly growing Gallatin Valley.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/king_arthur_park_montana",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The park’s eastern section hosts 210 sites, complete with a clubhouse, playground, and off‑street parking for residents.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://discoveringmontana.com/towns/king-arthur-park",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 2025, residents formed a tenants’ union after learning the park might be sold to a private equity firm.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/King_Arthur_Park%2C_Montana",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "editorial_filler"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "On May Day 2026, tenants launched a rent strike when owners refused to discuss a recent rent increase.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/King_Arthur_Park%2C_Montana",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "editorial_filler"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "King Arthur Park covers 200 acres, offering a mix of residential and community spaces.",
